  sources:
  - name: Becker et al. 2018 Basel carsharing
    authority: Henrik Becker, Francesco Ciari, Kay W. Axhausen (ETH Zürich, IVT)
    url: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trd.2018.08.003
    description: 'Measuring the car ownership impact of free-floating car-sharing
      - A case study in Basel, Switzerland. Transportation Research Part D 65:51-62
      (2018). Panel with a control group: -0.08 to -0.13 cars per member household
      in the first year. Archived: the working paper (IVT Arbeitsbericht 1176).; Attachment:
      source_material/car_ownership/becker_ciari_axhausen_ethz_ab1176_basel_ffcs_travel_behaviour.pdf;
      Format: Journal article; Geographic Coverage: Switzerland; Date Last Updated:
      2018-12-01; Updated by: Elsevier'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Bösch et al. 2018 autonomous mobility costs
    authority: Patrick M. Bösch, Felix Becker, Henrik Becker, Kay W. Axhausen 
      (ETH Zürich, IVT)
    url: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tranpol.2017.09.005
    description: 'Cost-based analysis of autonomous mobility services. Transport Policy
      64:76-91 (2018). Archived: the 2017 working paper (IVT Arbeitsberichte 1225).
      Automation raises the vehicle price by 20 % (IHS 2014); the driver is removed;
      a cleaning every 40 trips at 15 CHF; insurance -50 %.; Attachment: source_material/driverless/bosch_2017_ivt_ab1225_cost_autonomous_mobility.pdf;
      Format: Journal article; Geographic Coverage: Switzerland; Date Last Updated:
      2018-05-01; Updated by: Elsevier'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Composite traffic model v. 1.0.1 (Analytica)
    authority: Jouni T Tuomisto and Marko Tainio (National Public Health 
      Institute KTL)
    url: https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2458-5-123
    description: 'Additional file 1 of the article: CompositeTraffic_1_0_1.ana, Analytica
      3.1 XML, URN:NBN:fi-fe20051439. Trip data, road network, trip aggregation code,
      precomputed aggregation results for 85 scenarios (Scen1_0, Trips1_0), cost elements
      and decision analysis.; Attachment: source_material/12889_2005_278_MOESM1_ESM.ana;
      Format: Analytica model (XML); Licensing: CC BY 2.0; Geographic Coverage: Helsinki
      metropolitan area; Date Last Updated: 2005-11-03; Updated by: BioMed Central'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Composite traffic module plan
    authority: Jouni Tuomisto, Kausal
    url:
    description: 'The rollout paths of composite traffic, the path of driverless composite
      vehicles and the share of car users giving up their cars decided for the projection
      (paths-data modules/composite-traffic/docs/plan.md, Round 4; scripts/create_datasets.py,
      ROLLOUT_PATHS, DRIVERLESS_PATH; reference_decision_analysis.py, car_shedding).
      Assumptions, not observations.; Format: Plan; Geographic Coverage: Helsinki
      metropolitan area; Date Last Updated: 2026-11-28; Updated by: Kausal'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Cruise remote assistance 2023
    authority: CNBC / NBC Bay Area
    url: 
      https://www.nbcbayarea.com/news/business/money-report/cruise-confirms-robotaxis-rely-on-human-assistance-every-four-to-five-miles/3363333/
    description: "Cruise confirms robotaxis rely on human assistance every four to
      five miles (6 Nov 2023): 'roughly 1 remote assistant agent for every 15-20 driverless
      AVs', remote assistance in session 2-4 % of the time. A company statement.;
      Attachment: source_material/driverless/cruise_remote_assistance_2023.html; Format:
      News article; Geographic Coverage: United States; Date Last Updated: 2023-11-06;
      Updated by: CNBC"
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: ESMA carbon markets report 2026
    authority: European Securities and Markets Authority
    url: 
      https://www.esma.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2026-07/ESMA50-481369926-34622_Carbon_markets_report_2026.pdf
    description: '"The annual average price of EU emission allowances (EUAs) was EUR
      74 per tonne of CO2-equivalent ... in 2025."; Attachment: source_material/current_2025/esma_carbon_markets_report_2026.pdf;
      Format: PDF report; Geographic Coverage: EU; Date Last Updated: 2026-07-09;
      Updated by: ESMA'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: HSL travel survey 2023
    authority: Helsinki Region Transport (HSL)
    url: https://www.hsl.fi/en/hsl/research-and-surveys/travelsurvey2023
    description: 'Helsingin seudun asukkaiden arkipäivän matkat syksyllä 2023: trips
      per person and mode shares by municipality (Figures 2, 5, 6). Copy from a mirror,
      since hsl.fi refused automated download.; Attachment: source_material/current_2025/hsl_liikkumistutkimus_2023_kulkutapajakaumat.pdf;
      Format: PDF report; Geographic Coverage: Helsinki region; Date Last Updated:
      2024-06-01; Updated by: HSL'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Handbook on the external costs of transport 2019
    authority: CE Delft for the European Commission, DG MOVE
    url: 
      https://cedelft.eu/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2021/03/CE_Delft_4K83_Handbook_on_the_external_costs_of_transport_Final.pdf
    description: 'Version 2019-1.1. Value of a statistical life for the EU28 3.6 MEUR
      (2016 prices).; Attachment: source_material/current_2025/handbook_external_costs_of_transport_2019.pdf;
      Format: PDF report; Geographic Coverage: EU; Date Last Updated: 2020-01-01;
      Updated by: European Commission'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: ITF 2017 shared mobility Helsinki
    authority: International Transport Forum (OECD)
    url: 
      https://www.itf-oecd.org/sites/default/files/docs/shared-mobility-simulations-helsinki.pdf
    description: 'Shared Mobility Simulations for Helsinki (2017). Focus group: 3
      of 11 car owners would sell their car, only if the services covered the whole
      Helsinki metropolitan area.; Attachment: source_material/car_ownership/itf_2017_shared_mobility_simulations_helsinki.pdf;
      Format: Report; Geographic Coverage: Helsinki metropolitan area; Date Last Updated:
      2017-01-01; Updated by: ITF'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Martin & Shaheen 2011 carsharing
    authority: Elliot Martin, Susan Shaheen (UC Berkeley TSRC)
    url: https://escholarship.org/uc/item/7w58646d
    description: 'The Impact of Carsharing on Household Vehicle Ownership. ACCESS
      38 (2011); data as Martin, Shaheen & Lidicker, TRR 2143 (2010). 6,281 North
      American member households, 2008: vehicles per household 0.47 -> 0.24; carless
      households 62 % -> 80 %.; Attachment: source_material/car_ownership/martin_shaheen_2011_access38_carsharing_vehicle_ownership.pdf;
      Format: Journal article; Geographic Coverage: North America; Date Last Updated:
      2011-03-01; Updated by: UC Berkeley'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Martin & Shaheen 2016 car2go
    authority: Elliot Martin, Susan Shaheen (UC Berkeley TSRC)
    url: https://escholarship.org/uc/item/3mc5m6pn
    description: 'Impacts of car2go on vehicle ownership, modal shift, vehicle miles
      traveled, and greenhouse gas emissions (working paper 2016). Free-floating carsharing
      in five cities, 2-4 years after launch: 2-5 % of active members sold a car and
      7-10 % did not buy one.; Attachment: source_material/car_ownership/martin_shaheen_2016_car2go_impacts.pdf;
      Format: Working paper; Geographic Coverage: North America; Date Last Updated:
      2016-07-01; Updated by: UC Berkeley'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Nijland et al. 2015 car sharing
    authority: Hans Nijland, Jordy van Meerkerk, Anco Hoen (PBL)
    url: https://pbl.nl/downloads/pbl-2015-note-impact-of-car-sharing-1842pdf
    description: 'Impact of car sharing on mobility and CO2 emissions, PBL note (2015);
      peer-reviewed as Nijland & van Meerkerk, Environ. Innov. Soc. Transit. 23:84-91
      (2017). 363 Dutch car sharers: cars per household 0.85 -> 0.72; 1.08 -> 0.72
      against the cars they would have bought.; Attachment: source_material/car_ownership/pbl_2015_nijland_impact_of_car_sharing.pdf;
      Format: Report; Geographic Coverage: Netherlands; Date Last Updated: 2015-06-01;
      Updated by: PBL Netherlands Environmental Assessment Agency'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Statistics Finland consumer price index 11xt
